000 Feet/Gilpin/Clear Creek/Northeast Park Counties Below 9000 Feet; Larimer County Below 6000 Feet/Northwest Weld County; Boulder And Jefferson Counties Below 6000 Feet/West Broomfield County; North Douglas County Below 6000 Feet/Denver/West Adams and Arapahoe Counties/East Broomfield County; Elbert/Central and East Douglas Counties Above 6000 Feet; Northeast Weld County; Central and South Weld County; Morgan County; Central and East Adams and Arapahoe Counties; North and Northeast Elbert County Below 6000 Feet/North Lincoln County; Southeast Elbert County Below 6000 Feet/South Lincoln County; Logan County; Washington County; Sedgwick County; Phillips County","id":"urn:oid:2.49.0.1.840.0.eea7fe66bbe726127cab571e453d260029b0d72c.001.1","url":"https://api.weather.gov/alerts/urn:oid:2.49.0.1.840.0.eea7fe66bbe726127cab571e453d260029b0d72c.001.1"},{"event":"Flood Watch","headline":"Flood Watch issued August 15 at 11:32AM MDT until August 16 at 6:00AM MDT by NWS Goodland KS","description":"* WHAT...Flash flooding caused by excessive rainfall is possible.\n\n* WHERE...Portions of east central Colorado, including the following\narea, Cheyenne CO and west central Kansas, including the following\nareas, Gove, Greeley, Logan, Wallace and Wichita.\n\n* WHEN...From 6 PM MDT  /7 PM CDT/ this evening through late tonight.\n\n* IMPACTS...Excessive runoff may result in flooding of rivers,\ncreeks, streams, and other low-lying and flood-prone locations.\nLow-water crossings may be flooded.\n\n* ADDITIONAL DETAILS...\n- 1-3 inches of rain the past couple nights along with the\npotential for another cluster or two of storms this evening and\novernight increases the potential for some flooding and even\nflash flooding. Rainfall rates of 1.5 to 2.5 inches per hour is\npossible in the strongest cells.","ends":"2026-08-16T06:00:00-06:00","severity":"Severe","areaDesc":"Cheyenne County; Wallace; Logan; Gove; Greeley; Wichita","id":"urn:oid:2.49.0.1.840.0.e088e0765aa75bc050e847f792689803d87